attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a spine.** Columns 0 to 15, `mdtN` to `actP`, are carried by 91 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0.2 to 12% of calls {S1}. The model names 90 to 99% of them, fewest at column 4, `yjcO`, 90% {S1}.

@variable **A variable column breaks the spine at 16**, `espX5`, carried by 66% {S2.c16}. Then columns 17 to 20, `yjcE` to `soxS`, are [[superoxide response]] {S3, Q}. Through columns 61 to 67 a branch of 7 shell families runs in 26 to 30%, [[mannose and sorbose transport]] {S8.b61, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 95 against 91%, and hesitates less there, 0.23 against 0.41 bits {M}. It hesitates most at column 28, `yjbS`, a variable column, 1.08 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends in fork and variable columns.** Columns 35 to 79 are carried by 33 to 87% of chromosomes, in a region of plasticity in 12 to 36% of calls {S8}. The last column is `yjaG`, in 35% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 93% of genes**, 0.34 bits on average, perplexity 1.5 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 1.00 against 0.24 bits, and names fewer genes, 71% against 96% {C}.

